Negative control for the COMPLETE-CONTEXT law (`R6-30c` / `R6-30d`).

Hands the editor a context whose id was never found on the row — `undefined`
stringified — instead of opening a record that does not exist yet. The half-set
case the headless type makes unrepresentable is reintroduced at the one place
that builds a context from a row, so an Add-new control boots `.for()` against a
record id nobody supplied rather than `.fresh()`.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the list-surface handoff spec — the Add-new control opens the editor on a
NEW record (no context, booted fresh), and only a row-supplied id produces one.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
@@ -709,9 +709,7 @@
     // A context is only ever COMPLETE (`R6-30c`): no id off the row means a
     // record that does not exist yet, which the editor boots fresh.
     context:
-      handoff.context && !isNil(id)
-        ? { type: handoff.context.type, id: toString(id) }
-        : undefined
+      handoff.context && { type: handoff.context.type, id: toString(id) }
   };
 }
 
